ature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. If a creature enters the battlefield this way, it enters with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Return target artifact, enchantment, or planeswalker card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'Sacrifice Hajar, Loyal Bodyguard: Legendary creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain indestructible until end of turn.', 'Surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)\\nDraw a card.', 'Tap up to two target artifacts and/or creatures. Put two stun counters on each of them. (If a permanent with a stun counter would become untapped, remove one from it instead.)', 'Target artifact or creature gains hexproof and indestructible until end of turn. Scry 1.', 'Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains first strike and trample until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +2/+1 and gains lifelink until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', "Target creature you control gets +1/+2 until end of turn. It fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Target nonland permanent's owner puts it on the top or bottom of their library. Scry 2.", 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it. That player discards that card.\\nCreate a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose an artifact or creature card from it, then choose an artifact or creature card from their graveyard. Exile the chosen cards.', 'Teething Wurmlet has deathtouch as long as you control three or more artifacts.\\nWhenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life. If this is the first time this ability has resolved this turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Teething Wurmlet.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy target artifact. If its mana value was 1 or less, draw a card.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature card in your graveyard.\\nExile target creature or planeswalker.', "This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control an artifact creature.\\nReturn target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.", 'This spell costs {3} less to cast if it targets a creature card with mana value 3 or less.\\nReturn target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Trample\\nMishra's Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.\\nUnearth {5}{R} ({5}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", "Trample\\nPlayers can't gain life.", 'Trample\\nSteel Exemplar enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it unless two or more colors of mana were spent to cast it.', 'Trample\\nWhen Gnarlroot Pallbearer enters the battlefield, target creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', 'Trample\\nWhen you cast this spell and whenever Cityscape Leveler attacks, destroy up to one target nonland permanent. Its controller creates a tapped Powerstone token.\\nUnearth {8}', 'Trample\\nWhenever a land enters the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', "Unleash Shell deals 5 damage to target creature or planeswalker and 2 damage to that permanent's controller.", 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +2/+0 and gains "When this creature dies or is put into exile from the battlefield, return it to its owner\'s hand."', "Vigilance, reach, trample, haste\\nTitania, Gaea Incarnate's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.\\nWhen Titania enters the battlefield, return all land cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.\\n{3}{G}: Put four +1/+1 counters on target land you control. It becomes a 0/0 Elemental creature with haste. It's still a land.", "Vigilance\\nWard {4} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {4}.)\\nWhen Su-Chi Cave Guard dies, add eight {C}. Until end of turn, you don't lose this mana as steps and phases end.", 'Vigilance\\nWhen Loran of the Third Path enters the battlefield, destroy up to one target artifact or enchantment.\\n{T}: You and target opponent each draw a card.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, Phalanx Vanguard gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Vigilance\\n{1}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\nWhenever you discard one or more artifact cards, create a tapped Powerstone token. This ability triggers only once each turn. (The token is an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'Ward {2} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {2}.)', 'Ward—Pay 2 life. (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays 2 life.)\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'When Arbalest Engineers enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Arbalest Engineers deals 1 damage to any target.\\n• Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature. It gains trample and haste until end of turn.\\n• Create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'When Argothian Opportunist enters the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'When Bitter Reunion enters the battlefield, you may discard a card. If you do, draw two cards.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Bitter Reunion: Creatures you control gain haste until end of turn.', 'When Bladecoil Serpent enters the battlefield, for each {U}{U} spent to cast it, draw a card.\\nWhen Bladecoil Serpent enters the battlefield, for each {B}{B} spent to cast it, each opponent discards a card.\\nWhen Bladecoil Serpent enters the battlefield, for each {R}{R} spent to cast it, it gets +1/+0 and gains trample and haste until end of turn.', "When Blanchwood Prowler enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put a land card from among the cards milled this way into your hand. If you don't, put a +1/+1 counter on Blanchwood Prowler. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)", 'When Burrowing Razormaw dies, mill four cards. (Put the top four cards of your library into your graveyard.)', 'When Conscripted Infantry dies, create a 1/1 colorless Soldier artifact creature token.', 'When Disciples of Gix enters the battlefield, search your library for up to three artifact cards, put them into your graveyard, then shuffle.', 'When Energy Refractor enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{2}: Add one mana of any color.', "When Evangel of Synthesis enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.\\nAs long as you've drawn two or more cards this turn, Evangel of Synthesis gets +1/+0 and has menace.", "When Fallaji Archaeologist enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put a noncreature, nonland card from among the cards milled this way into your hand. If you don't, put a +1/+1 counter on Fallaji Archaeologist. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)", "When Gnawing Vermin enters the battlefield, target player mills two cards.\\nWhen Gnawing Vermin dies, target creature you don't control gets -1/-1 until end of turn.", 'When Great Desert Prospector enters the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token for each other creature you control. (The tokens are artifacts with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'When Haywire Mite dies, you gain 2 life.\\n{G}, Sacrifice Haywire Mite: Exile target noncreature artifact or noncreature enchantment.', 'When Hero of the Dunes enters the battlefield, return target artifact or creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nCreatures you control with mana value 3 or less get +1/+0.', 'When Junkyard Genius enters the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")\\n{1}{B}{R}, Sacrifice another creature or artifact: Until end of turn, other creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain menace and haste.', 'When Obstinate Baloth enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.\\nIf a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Obstinate Baloth, put it onto the battlefield instead of putting it into your graveyard.', "When Portal to Phyrexia enters the battlefield, each opponent sacrifices three creatures.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. It's a Phyrexian in addition to its other types.", 'When Powerstone Engineer dies, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', "When Ravenous Gigamole enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put a creature card from among the cards milled this way into your hand. If you don't, put a +1/+1 counter on Ravenous Gigamole. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)", 'When Scrapwork Cohort enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 colorless Soldier artifact creature token.\\nUnearth {2}{W} ({2}{W}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Scrapwork Mutt enters the battlefield, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\\nUnearth {1}{R} ({1}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Scrapwork Rager enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.\\nUnearth {3}{B} ({3}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Simian Simulacrum enters the battlefield, put two +1/+1 counters on target creature you control.\\nUnearth {2}{G}{G} ({2}{G}{G}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Static Net enters the battlefield, exile target nonland permanent an opponent controls until Static Net leaves the battlefield.\\nWhen Static Net enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life and create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'When Stone Retrieval Unit enters the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', "When The Mightstone and Weakstone enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Draw two cards.\\n• Target creature gets -5/-5 until end of turn.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}. This mana can't be spent to cast nonartifact spells.\\n(Melds with Urza, Lord Protector.)", "When Tocasia's Onulet leaves the battlefield, you gain 2 life.\\nUnearth {3}{W} ({3}{W}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", "When Tomakul Scrapsmith enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put an artifact card from among the cards milled this way into your hand. If you don't, put a +1/+1 counter on Tomakul Scrapsmith. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)", "Whenever Ashnod's Harvester attacks, exile target card from a graveyard.\\nUnearth {1}{B} ({1}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", "Whenever Gaea's Courser attacks, if there are three or more creature cards in your graveyard, draw a card.", 'Whenever Kill-Zone Acrobat attacks, you may sacrifice another creature or artifact. If you do, Kill-Zone Acrobat gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever Loran, Disciple of History or another legendary creature enters the battlefield under your control, return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Whenever Mishra, Lost to Phyrexia enters the battlefield or attacks, choose three —\\n• Target opponent discards two cards.\\n• Mishra deals 3 damage to any target.\\n• Destroy target artifact or planeswalker.\\n• Creatures you control gain menace and trample until end of turn.\\n• Creatures you don't control get -1/-1 until end of turn.\\n• Create two tapped Powerstone tokens.", 'Whenever Slagstone Refinery or another nontoken artifact you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield or is put into exile from the battlefield, create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', 'Whenever Terisian Mindbreaker attacks, defending player mills half their library, rounded up.\\nUnearth {1}{U}{U}{U} ({1}{U}{U}{U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever Yotian Frontliner attacks, another target creature you control gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nUnearth {W} ({W}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', "Whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents, its controller may pay 1 life. If they do, they draw a card.\\n{4}{B}{B}{B}, Discard X cards: Exile the top X cards of target opponent's library. You may play lands and cast spells from among cards exiled this way without paying their mana costs.", 'Whenever a creature with power equal to its toughness enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, Perimeter Patrol gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may reveal it and put it into your hand. If you don't put the card into your hand, you may put it into your graveyard.", 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.', 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player loses 5 life unless they discard a card.', 'Whenever one or more artifact and/or creature cards leave your graveyard during your turn, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.', 'Whenever one or more creatures with mana value 3 or less enter the battlefield under your control, draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'Whenever you attack, each opponent loses X life and you gain X life, where X is the number of attacking creatures. If Mishra, Claimed by Gix and a creature named Phyrexian Dragon Engine are attacking, and you both own and control them, exile them, then meld them into Mishra, Lost to Phyrexia. It enters the battlefield tapped and attacking.', 'Whenever you cast a Beast or Bird creature spell, you may copy it, except the copy is an artifact in addition to its other types. (The copy becomes a token.)', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, create a 1/1 colorless Soldier artifact creature token.', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a loyalty counter on Teferi, Temporal Pilgrim.\\n[0]: Draw a card.\\n[−2]: Create a 2/2 blue Spirit creature token with vigilance and "Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature."\\n[−12]: Target opponent chooses a permanent they control and returns it to its owner\'s hand. Then they shuffle each nonland permanent they control into its owner\'s library.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, each opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.\\nWhen Gixian Puppeteer dies, return another target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Lat-Nam Adept.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Thopter Mechanic.\\nWhen Thopter Mechanic dies, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you sacrifice another permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on Gixian Infiltrator.', 'You gain 1 life for each creature on the battlefield. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn by creatures with power 3 or less.', 'You may activate the loyalty abilities of Urza, Planeswalker twice each turn rather than only once.\\n[+2]: Artifact, instant, and sorcery spells you cast this turn cost {2} less to cast. You gain 2 life.\\n[+1]: Draw two cards, then discard a card.\\n[0]: Create two 1/1 colorless Soldier artifact creature tokens.\\n[−3]: Exile target nonland permanent.\\n[−10]: Artifacts and planeswalkers you control gain indestructible until end of turn. Destroy all nonland permanents.', 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may play lands and cast spells from the top of your library.\\nOnce during each of your turns, you may cast a spell from your hand or the top of your library without paying its mana cost.', 'You may play lands from your graveyard.\\nUnearth {G}{G} ({G}{G}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '[+1]: Scry 1. You may tap an untapped artifact you control. If you do, draw a card.\\n[−2]: Create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying. They gain haste until end of turn.\\n[−4]: You get an emblem with "Artifact creatures you control get +1/+1" and "Artifact spells you cast cost {1} less to cast."', '{1}, Sacrifice an artifact: Penregon Strongbull gets +1/+1 until end of turn and deals 1 damage to each opponent.', "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mishra's Research Desk: Exile the top two cards of your library. Choose one of them. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.\\nUnearth {1}{R} ({1}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)", '{1}: Until end of turn, Argivian Avenger gets -1/-1 and gains your choice of flying, vigilance, deathtouch, or haste.', "{1}{U}: Return target artifact you control to its owner's hand.\\n{3}, {T}: Copy target artifact spell you control. (The copy becomes a token.)", '{2}, Sacrifice Combat Courier: Draw a card.\\nUnearth {U} ({U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '{2}, {T}, Exile The Stasis Coffin: You gain protection from everything until your next turn.', "{2}, {T}, Exile The Stone Brain: Choose a card name. Search target opponent's graveyard, hand, and library for up to four cards with that name and exile them. That player shuffles, then draws a card for each card exiled from their hand this way. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{2}: Fallaji Chaindancer gains double strike until end of turn.', '{2}: Retrieval Agent gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', '{2}{G}: Until end of turn, target noncreature artifact you control becomes a 4/4 artifact creature.', "{2}{W}: Return target permanent you control to its owner's hand. If it has unearth, instead exile it, then return that card to its owner's hand. Activate only during your turn.", "{2}{W}{W}, {T}, Exile Urza's Sylex: Each player chooses six lands they control. Destroy all other permanents. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nWhen Urza's Sylex is put into exile from the battlefield, you may pay {2}. If you do, search your library for a planeswalker card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", '{3}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature or artifact: Draw a card.', '{3}: Power Plant Worker gets +2/+2 until end of turn. If you control creatures named Mine Worker and Tower Worker, put two +1/+1 counters on Power Plant Worker instead. Activate only once each turn.', "{3}: Put target artifact, instant, or sorcery card from a graveyard on the bottom of its owner's library.", '{3}: Target Soldier gains flying until end of turn.', '{3}{R}: You may put an artifact card from your hand onto the battlefield. That artifact gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', '{3}{W}: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature card with mana value 3 or less from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', '{4}, {T}: Discard all the cards in your hand, then draw that many cards. You may choose an artifact or creature card with mana value 1 you discarded this way, then do the same for artifact or creature cards with mana values 2 and 3. Return those cards to the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{5}, {T}: Each opponent loses 2 life. This ability costs {1} less to activate for each creature card in your graveyard.', '{7}: Draw two cards.', '{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Add {C}{C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Create a 3/3 colorless Zombie artifact creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{G}, {T}, Discard a creature card: Search your library for a creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Tap an untapped artifact or creature you control: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add X mana of any one color, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add two mana in any combination of colors. Spend this mana only to cast creature spells or activate abilities of a creature or creature card.\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell with power 5 or greater, put a +1/+1 counter on Gwenna, Eyes of Gaea and untap it.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{4}, {T}: Create a tapped Powerstone token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can\'t be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.")', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Demolition Field: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls. That land's controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. You may search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}: Mishra's Foundry becomes a 2/2 Assembly-Worker artifact creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{1}, {T}: Target attacking Assembly-Worker gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Llanowar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: You gain 1 life. If you control creatures named Power Plant Worker and Tower Worker, you gain 3 life instead.', '{X}, {T}, Sacrifice Mask of the Jadecrafter: Create an X/X colorless Golem artifact creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nUnearth {2}{G} ({2}{G}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)']
flavor: ['"Achieving perfection is simple. Watch, I\'ll do it twice."\\n—Mishra', '"Aha! This must be one of the ancient keys to... No, wait. It\'s just another puzzle toy."', '"And if this works, Tawnos is gonna let us build the full-sized version!"\\n—Tergel, goblin explosioneer', '"Any more giant metal monsters want to try their luck? I\'m just getting warmed up!"', '"Artifice is not the only form of creation."\\n—Titania', '"As Terisiare\'s mines ran dry, scrap metal became increasingly plentiful."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"As usual, my brother\'s maneuvers are brash and impulsive."\\n—Urza', '"At heart, Urza was an inventor, not a warlord. Over time, the burdens of leadership left him as cold and calculating as his mechanical creations."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"Automatons are fast, precise, and tireless, but they all share one weakness: predictability. Learn their patterns. Strike when they\'re vulnerable."\\n—Horance, Urzan general', '"Back to the ivory towers! This won\'t hold for long!"\\n—Vayor, Third Path cryomancer', '"Don\'t excavate too far into those canyons. I promised your parents I\'d return you in one piece."\\n—Tocasia', '"Don\'t thank me. Thank nature for its wondrous designs!"', '"Even the leaves oppose your being here. What hope have you against nature\'s might?"', '"Every book is a doorway to enlightenment. Curiosity is your key."', '"Every name on this list is already a hero! Will you add your own to it?"', '"Everyone warns about the sand and the food, but the rats are worse than both put together!"\\n—Sanwell, letter to his family', '"Focus your mind. Do you hold a piece of the ocean or a thousand drops of rain?"\\n—Hurkyl', '"For the love of the seven brass gods, it\'s a city of academics! How are they doing this?"\\n—Sharaman, Urzan lieutenant', '"Forge the future in metal and oil!"', '"Funny," remarked Laga to his squad. "Mishra\'s lackeys wear luxurious silks in their gilded palaces, while we toil in the trenches eating stale bread."', '"Get the sylex to Urza at any cost. Tell him to fill it with memories of the land."\\n—Ashnod, to Tawnos', '"Go, save as many as you can! The city walls may be rubble, but Kroog will live on in its people."\\n—Queen Kayla bin-Kroog', '"Hah. Urza has underestimated my strength yet again."\\n—Mishra', '"Hear that thud-clank, thud-clank? We\'re saved."\\n—Ani, Urzan soldier', '"Hello, beautiful."', '"I call on both predators and protectors, for now is a season of war."', '"I joined this war to protect my homeland, not to destroy someone else\'s."', '"I need an army, not a masterpiece. Accelerate output, whatever it takes."\\n—Urza, notes to his engineers', '"I will trust desert steel in Fallaji hands over a soulless machine any day."\\n—Hajar, Mishra\'s bodyguard', '"I\'ve stood by Mishra\'s side from the beginning. I will not abandon him now."', '"Imagine being scared of pixies. Just smoosh them under your boot!"\\n—Kerish, Urzan mechanist', '"It would be folly to fight a dragon engine head-on. Let\'s hit it from above."', '"Landing zone is clear. Activate and deploy!"', '"Listen, Duck. Gix is everywhere, playing every side. Mishra won\'t listen . . . but perhaps Urza will."', '"Machines feel no fear, no sorrow, no hunger—only glorious purpose, true and pure."', '"Make the exhaust vents smaller next time!"\\n—Urza, notes to his engineers', '"Most wise, most thoughtful, most powerful qadir," said the Gixian, "we offer whatever help we may give in your illustrious name."', '"Move! When the powerstone blows, that behemoth will be nothing but a hole in the ground."\\n—Ashnod, to Hajar', '"Nature adapts. So should we."', '"Never track the roc itself with your eyes, for it will swoop with the sun at its back and blind you. Instead, track its shadow and, when it\'s almost upon you, heave your javelin upward with all your might."', '"One down, several thousand more to go."', '"Put your backs into it! If we don\'t lay claim to it, the Fallaji will!"', '"Raw energy contains infinite possibility."\\n—Urza', '"Remember, students, if it\'s glowing, humming, or whirring, don\'t touch it!"', '"She\'ll only fly once. Make it count!"', '"Show me all the delicious misery you\'ve sown."', '"Steady, recruit. We fight in the light of justice. We cast no shadow."', '"Terisia City\'s fall is inevitable. My master\'s plan runs as sure and steady as the oil in my veins."', '"That\'s odd. I don\'t remember seeing plans to dig a trench near here."\\n—Lognell, Argivian scout', '"The Burnished Banner will show the Warlord that the Suwwardi Marches belong to the Fallaji!"', '"The Warlord thinks we\'ve gone soft, does he? The Fist of Progress will prove him wrong!"', '"The brothers are brilliant, but their quarreling will be the death of me."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', '"The ground is where wars are waged, but the air is where they are won."\\n—Harbin, vanguard aviator', '"The human body—like any other machine—can be stripped for parts."\\n—Ashnod', '"The sylex blast marked not only the end of the war, but the end of Dominaria as most knew it."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"The war polluted the land, turning what had once been fruitful fields into fetid morasses of mud and rusted corpses."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"The welds are weaker at the top."', '"There\'s a certain beauty in destruction. Some will consider this war a masterpiece."\\n—Ashnod', '"They\'re easy enough to squish, but they\'re a pain to wash out of a workbench."\\n—Tergel, goblin explosioneer', '"This metal belonged to Argoth before it was ripped from the ground. Now it belongs to Argoth again."', '"This metal junk is ugly, but it\'s got its uses."', '"Throw the bodies out. They\'ll just weigh down the frame."\\n—Rolf, Argivian mechanic', '"Time for the Iron Alliance to remind the qadir\'s army how inhospitable the Sword Marches can be."', '"Today our blades remember Kroog! May the seven brass gods be with us!"', '"Urza fortified every thirty miles on the path to Tomakul, creating a network of trenches the brothers would trade for decades."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"We expected the Argothians to stand their ground. We didn\'t expect the ground itself to stand."\\n—Myrel, Shield of Argive', '"Well there\'s your problem—resonance leak lowering output by thirty percent. I can patch that up."', '"Well? What are you waiting for? Let\'s not keep the buzzards waiting."', '"What you call magic, I call the power of memory."', '"When all you have is a hammer, everything looks like a nail. I merely propose expanding our toolbox."', '"With every culling, we bring this world closer to *compleation*."', '"With the Brotherhood of Gix whispering in his ear, Mishra\'s drive to prove himself was slowly twisted into an insatiable hunger for power."\\n-*The Antiquities War*', '"Yotia is my birthright, father. Let me fight for it."', '"You know those seedpods cluttering the eastern approach? I\'ve got an idea . . . ."\\n—Calle, Urzan sergeant', '"You want it good, fast, or cheap? You can\'t have all three."', '"You want me to install a seat belt? Please. You\'re lucky to get a seat!"', '"You\'ve let yourself grow old, and your light is dimming. Shall we talk one last time, or must I slay you now?"\\n—Mishra, to Urza', '"Your father was a dear friend to whom I owe much. He wanted me to look after you, to care for you should something happen to him."', 'A thousand years of growth, harvested in minutes.', 'After a long hibernation, Argoth began slowly recovering from the ravages of war.', 'After five thousand years, the nightmare returned.', 'Alongside his wife, Hurkyl, Drafna built a legacy of scholarship that endured for millennia.', 'Anyone can destroy a continent. Few have the vision to rebuild one.', "As Mishra's army bore down on Terisia City, Corlo felt his focus, his patience, and his willpower twine together. With a deep breath, he plucked answers from the air.", "As Terisia City burned, Feldon pressed the sylex into Loran's hands and urged her to run. Hope ran with her.", 'As a scholar, she saw the sylex not as a weapon, but as a key to the past.', "As retaliation for the Warlord's ambush at the peace summit, Mishra leveled Yotia's capital city.", "As the glowing stone broke apart, so too did the last shred of the brothers' bond.", "At first, the merchant state of Korlis saw no need to involve itself in the conflict between Yotia and the Fallaji. Mishra's dragon engines changed that.", 'Automatons could be rebuilt. Powerstones could not.', "Before Kaya could pull Teferi's spirit back, the overloaded temporal anchor failed, and he was set adrift in the currents of time.", 'Bravery outlives the brave.', 'Built to crush walls and wills in equal measure.', 'Dying for the cause is overrated.', "Each fallen friend was a seed of regret, eager to blossom again in Gaea's name.", "Even Urza's most mundane creations shared his obsession with perfection.", "Fallaji soldiers hated seeing loved ones' faces among the transmogrants. Ashnod devised a solution.", 'Few relics excited Fallaji archaeologists more than Thran powerstones, which they called "eyes of the Old Ones."', 'First one, then a second, then a third of the ivory towers fell to the invaders, who moved in a circle around the city like an apocalyptic clock.', 'First the automatons reinforced depleted squads. Then they replaced them entirely.', "Following his hunger for knowledge and power from the past, Urza starved Dominaria's future.", 'From above, the brothers noticed strange glyphs etched into the desert sand.', "Gix pierced his disciples' minds and savored their experiences as he took in their knowledge.", 'Glacian built his automatons to last, and last they did, beyond even the Thran themselves.', "Gwenna stayed her hand only once, to save young Harbin's life—a mistake she would never repeat.", 'Her circus training proved surprisingly valuable on the battlefield.', 'His child-lifting act was second only to his cauldron-punting routine.', 'History forgot her name but not her victories.', "In Mishra's desperation to destroy his brother, he allowed Gix to destroy him instead.", 'In desperation, Pero called on his memory of a lightning storm that nearly killed his family. When he opened his eyes, only smoke and dust remained.', 'In the Great Desert, one law is enforced over all others: water belongs to all.', 'In the ruins of Kroog, only anguish thrived.', "In war, dragons don't see sides, just side dishes.", "Inspired by fishing raptors, Tawnos designed the drake's talons to seize prey with overwhelming speed and precision.", 'It brings the two things weary soldiers need most: medicine and morale.', 'It can hear a panicked heartbeat from a thousand paces away.', 'It felt the rumblings of war and uncoiled itself from the depths of the world.', 'Mechanical workers toiled away, tirelessly fueling the impossible.', 'Mishra was gone—all that remained was a machine wearing his face.', "Mishra's army demanded the secrets of the Third Path. Hurkyl's followers graciously showed them.", "Mishra's nightmares of Phyrexia rang with screams of agony and groans of twisted metal. The sounds stayed with him long after he awoke.", 'Most goblins can light a fuse and run, but only the cleverest remember to drop the bomb.', 'New armaments, fresh provisions, and best of all, dry socks.', 'No honor. No glory. No leftovers.', 'Once the brothers discovered the pristine island of Argoth, the war came down to who could plunder it faster.', 'Only the quartermaster wept for their loss.', "Power radiated from the Weakstone, binding the dragon engine to Mishra's command.", 'Reports differed on whether the figure was an automaton or a mage, mostly because few who saw it survived.', 'Scurrying repair bots quietly turned the tide of many battles, patching damaged automatons back into fighting form.', "Sent by their noble parents to toughen up and learn something of the world's past, Urza and Mishra instead uncovered Terisiare's future.", 'She always leads the charge.', "She focused her mind on the volcano's fury, and hers erupted in kind.", 'She was eager to show the invading Yotians how she earned her nickname, "The Sandstorm of Tomakul."', "She'll swing a blade all her life, but never again for war.", "So thick was the fog on Argoth's shores that the brothers' forces passed within shouting distance of each other without realizing it.", 'Some armor is forged, some is forested.', "Tawnos built his clay statues for durability, not knowing they'd keep fighting long after the war.", 'Tawnos built it to be absolutely impermeable to any force inside. Luckily it worked for any force outside as well.', "Teferi's body couldn't travel through time far enough, but with Kaya's help, his spirit could.", 'Terisia City at last opened its ivory towers to all who sought respite from the endless war.', 'The Fallaji quickly learned that the Kher Ridges held too many caves and valleys to be surveyed from the air alone.', "The Thran's machines were not dead after all, merely dormant . . . and waiting.", 'The Warlord decreed that only someone who could move the statue would be strong enough to marry the princess. So Urza moved it.', 'The battlefield became so pockmarked with craters and trenches that casualties were regularly attributed to "fell in a hole."', "The brothers' rivalry escalated into all-out enmity, and Tocasia paid the price.", 'The cool, sleek automatons beside her mirrored her own iron resolve.', "The endless grind of the Brothers' War had fouled Terisiare's land and blackened its skies. Argoth's defenders were determined to protect their isle from the same fate.", "The flames of war consumed most of Argoth's treefolk. Vengeance consumed the rest.", 'The humming tome burned his leather glove, nearly taking his hand along with it. Then a strange power coursed through him.', "The metal turned and blossomed with Saheeli's will, each filigreed twist bringing the temporal anchor closer to completion.", "The new cannon's destructive power more than made up for its unpredictable blast radius.", 'The peace summit proved the grudge between Urza and Mishra could end only in blood.', "The prince consort was happy to let Yotia's coffers fund his extravagant research.", "The sylex's blast had razed the land, leaving behind only snow and sorrow. Urza stood alone in the sudden silence.", 'Though neither brother cared to admit it, flying the ancient thopter was their last happy moment together.', 'To some, desecration. To Gix, decoration.', 'To the spiders of Argoth, thopters were just bigger, crunchier flies.', "Tocasia's face haunted his vision. The explosion still rung in his ears. Mishra kept running and never once looked back.", 'Unable to settle on just one versatile being, Urza decided to create myriad adaptable machines.', "Urza and Mishra may have been Tocasia's most famous students, but Loran was the true heir to her legacy.", "Urza and Mishra weren't the only denizens of Terisiare to covet the powerstones' energy.", "Urza's engineers could take weeks to dig out a powerstone. The goblins weren't so painstaking.", 'Volunteers rarely questioned why the airborne battalion always seemed to be recruiting.', 'War prisoners were ineffective political pawns, as neither brother cared enough to trade for them.', 'When Titania offered peace, Urza merely turned her down. Mishra made her people pay for the insult.', 'When Urza betrayed the Sardian dwarves, they called upon the might of their neighbors for aid.', "When it came to fighting an army of trees, even Mishra's best generals were stumped.", 'While Urza read books, Mishra learned to read the desert itself.', "While Urza's machines favored defense, Mishra built his to end the war quickly.", 'While his master tried to surpass nature, Tawnos aimed to capture its beauty.', "With a snap of metal like a strike of lightning, the tide of war shifted in Mishra's favor."]
